  "notes": "Issue #465. Two independently-trained XGBoost models on EXP-374's exact feature build (same parser, hotspots, pathway families, canonical 5-fold/seed, EXP-374's fixed hyperparameters, no Optuna), each restricted by column mask to one #292 shift-AUC family: Model A uses only \"hotspot__*\" columns (fixed_hotspot family, shift-AUC ~0.55), Model B uses only \"sample__*\" columns (sample_aggregate_burden family -- robust burden aggregates plus fixed-pathway burden/composition, shift-AUC ~0.73). Blended 0.5/0.5. Unlike EXP-450/EXP-457/EXP-464 (same feature set, different models), this pair has different feature sets and different shift sensitivity, so a different failure mechanism (or success) is possible. Mandatory train_domain_propensity.csv test-like subset check (same boundary as EXP-351/EXP-450/EXP-457/EXP-464) is the primary judgment criterion."
